    <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
        <div class="mb-8"><p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[.17em] text-blue-700">Lumenix public website and platform</p><h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#102338]">Service terms</h1><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Effective date: 22 November 2026</p></div>
        <article class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-10">
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">1. About the service</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Lumenix provides an ISP operations platform for workspace management, subscriber billing records, payment workflows, MikroTik/FreeRADIUS workflows, service monitoring and reporting. Features and availability can depend on the ISP’s subscription, configuration, connected providers and network equipment.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">2. ISP applications and accounts</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">An ISP applicant must provide accurate business and owner details. Public workspace applications are reviewed before operational access is approved. Platform administrators may create workspaces directly. Each ISP is responsible for its staff accounts, assigned roles, passwords, router credentials and activity performed in its workspace.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">3. Two independent billing relationships</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Subscriber invoices and payments belong to the ISP’s customer relationship. The ISP sets subscriber packages and is responsible for its prices, invoices, collection accounts, refunds, credits and customer communications. Separately, Lumenix bills the ISP for platform subscription fees. The applicable base plan, included active-subscriber allowance, router limit, currency and ISP-specific overage rate are shown in platform subscription details and invoices.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Where an overage rate applies, the platform calculation uses the active subscriber count for the billing period, subtracts the plan’s included allowance, and multiplies the remaining count by the per-subscriber rate configured for that ISP. The generated platform invoice is the record of the amount due.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">4. Payments and internet access</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">A payment confirmation can settle an invoice and update a subscription, but payment alone does not confirm that a subscriber has internet access. Router availability, RADIUS provisioning, accounting data and live connectivity are separate operational states. ISPs are responsible for checking service delivery and resolving network or provider failures.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">5. Acceptable use and network configuration</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">ISPs must use the service lawfully, maintain permission to manage their networks and customer records, and protect access to their routers and third-party payment accounts. Do not use the platform to access systems or data without authorization, disrupt other customers, or submit fraudulent payment or identity information. Router and provider integrations must be configured with credentials and endpoints the ISP is authorized to use.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">6. Third-party services and availability</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">M-Pesa/Daraja, email delivery, MikroTik devices, FreeRADIUS and connectivity providers may be operated by third parties. Their availability, terms and behavior are outside Lumenix’s direct control. Integrations and telemetry depend on correct configuration, network reachability and supported provider behavior. No uptime commitment is made here; any service level commitment must be agreed separately in writing.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">7. Data, suspension and records</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">The ISP remains responsible for the lawfulness and accuracy of subscriber information it enters. Workspace suspension may restrict access while preserving data and historical records. Posted financial records and audit history may be retained for operational and legal recordkeeping even if a workspace is suspended or closed. See the <a class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline" href="{{ route('marketing.privacy') }}">Privacy notice</a>.</p></section>
            <section><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#102338]">8. Changes and questions</h2><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Plan-specific billing terms are reflected in the ISP’s subscription and invoices. Lumenix may update platform features or these public terms; material subscription changes should be reflected in platform notices or updated subscription details. For service, pricing or terms questions, use the <a class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline" href="{{ route('home') }}#contact">Lumenix contact form</a>.@if(filled($supportEmail)) You can also email <a class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline" href="mailto:{{ $supportEmail }}">{{ $supportEmail }}</a>.@endif</p></section>
